<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elisabeth Farnese</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1692">1692</a>–1766</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elisabeth Farnese (1692–1766) was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> as the second wife of Philip V from 1714, and heiress of the Farnese dukes of Parma. A dominant figure at the Spanish court, she used war and diplomacy to win Italian thrones for her sons, securing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> for Charles and Parma for Philip.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elisabeth-farnese.jpg" alt="Elisabeth Farnese" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis-Michel van Loo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isabel_de_Farnesio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
